{% if sandbar_profile_type | default('') %}
- Connection profile type: `{{ sandbar_profile_type }}`.
{% else %}
- Connection profile type: not recorded. A `/mnt/lima-cidata` directory
  suggests Lima (`local` or `remote-ssh`); ask the user which.
{% endif %}

Profile types:

- `local`: Lima on the user's workstation. Guest ports appear on the
  workstation's `localhost`.
- `remote-ssh`: Lima on another machine the workstation reaches over SSH.
  Guest ports appear on that machine's loopback, not the workstation's.
- `proxmox`: a Proxmox VE VM with its own network address.

{% if ddev_router_https_port is defined %}
ddev ports on this VM (set in `~/.ddev/global_config.yaml`; they differ from
other VMs' and from ddev's defaults):

- Router: HTTP {{ ddev_router_http_port }}, HTTPS {{ ddev_router_https_port }}.
- Mailpit: HTTP {{ ddev_mailpit_http_port }}, HTTPS {{ ddev_mailpit_https_port }}.
- XHGui: HTTP {{ ddev_xhgui_http_port }}, HTTPS {{ ddev_xhgui_https_port }}.
- Traefik monitor: {{ ddev_traefik_monitor_port }}.

Project sites are at `https://<project>.ddev.site:{{ ddev_router_https_port }}`;
the port is part of the URL.
{% else %}
ddev ports: not set by Sandbar for this VM, so ddev uses its default ports
(80/443) or is not configured. Check `ddev config global` if it matters.
{% endif %}

See [ports.md](ports.md) for what each means for reaching a guest server.
